'''Semiconductor etching''' is the controlled removal of selected material from a semiconductor wafer to transfer a patterned geometry into a film or substrate. Etching may use liquid-phase chemistry (wet etching) or gas/plasma-based chemistry (dry etching). It follows pattern definition but is not synonymous with [[Photolithography]].
